# sha256 of data/willeq.db, the shipped SQLite database. Rebuilt by
# scripts/build_willeq_db.sh from eight inputs: the EQ client's spells_us.txt,
# eqstr_us.txt, dbstr_us.txt, SoundAssets.txt, AnimationSounds.txt,
# mp3index.txt, plus data/item_models.json and
# config/race_models.json. 28,321 rows across nine tables,
# metadata.version = 7 (kWilleqDbExpectedVersion).
#
# T454 (board B474) dropped the twelfth table, equipment_textures (2,623 rows
# nothing read), and T456 (board B476) dropped the eleventh, equipment_models
# (1,000 rows, nothing read either) -- together the whole of the difference
# from T450's 32,414. B606 (#189) dropped the tenth, login_strings (470 rows,
# its only client reader getLoginString() had zero production callers).
# The equipment model AND texture paths both resolve LIVE,
# through EquipmentModelLoader::buildEquipmentIndex(); neither table was a
# broken route, both were redundant ones.
#
# metadata.input_digest moved with every input-set change: c39f5cfbb75e5744
# (T450's ten inputs) -> 956f69a5686c98bb (T456's nine) ->
# 10ec9bedbe6c7c5e (B606's eight: eqlsstr_us.txt went with the
# login_strings table). T454 changed only the loader, so its nine inputs
# hashed the same; T456 removed data/equipment_models.json from the input
# set itself. The digest is over the inputs, so dropping one must move it.
#
# T450 (board B467) made the file reproducible in the first place: the builder
# used to stamp metadata.build_date = __DATE__ " " __TIME__, so recompiling it
# changed these bytes with identical inputs and no pin was possible. That row
# is now metadata.input_digest, a path-independent digest of the inputs.
#
# B1103 (GitLab #423) moved the sha WITHOUT moving the input digest: the
# input set is unchanged (eight inputs, same contents), only the LOADER
# changed -- spells.spell_icon now carries field 144 (NEW_ICON, the client's
# spell icon) instead of field 143 (ai_pt_bonus, 0 on every row), so the
# spellbook's icon column is the client's own instead of the all-zero
# phantom. The gem_icon column (also field 144) is byte-identical to before.
#
# Pinned here so an input drift, or a hand-edit of the database, is a ctest
# FAIL (DbReproducible). Update this line in the SAME commit that changes an
# input -- exactly like data/willeq.eqe1.sha256 and data/textures.sha256.
9638cc5ade776fa1b6fa9b5caae8baa666841696fed418de9cf70a56f0361e14  data/willeq.db
